prompt_template:
Create a finished raster editorial poster in the "Burnt Orange Halftone Hero Collage" visual style.

STYLE FIDELITY IS THE FIRST PRIORITY. Make every one of these anchors visibly present: {STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}

SOURCE CONTENT MUST CHANGE. Do not recreate any of the following literal content: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

New content:
- Hero subject: {SUBJECT}
- Action: {SUBJECT_ACTION}
- Secondary prop: {PRODUCT_OR_PROP}
- Setting: {LOCATION}
- Background diagram and silhouette material: {BACKGROUND_ELEMENTS}
- Exact giant headline text: {MAIN_TEXT}
- Exact small kicker and footer text: {SECONDARY_TEXT}
- Original accent emblem: {ACCENT_SYMBOL}
- Wardrobe and styling: {WARDROBE_STYLE}

Build a dense edge-to-edge editorial collage in shallow planar layers, not a realistic scene. Use this back-to-front stack: warm uncoated cream paper; one enormous extra-heavy condensed uppercase headline in burnt orange spanning nearly the full width; a burnt-orange rectangular panel with white halftone diagrams; one dominant warm flash-lit full-color photographic hero cutout centered with a slight right bias and occupying 60 to 70 percent of the canvas height; one smaller overlapping prop in the lower-left quadrant; one rough black dry-brush word sweep across the upper middle; one newly invented oversized looping orange line with a black keyline across the foreground; one edge-to-edge black-and-cream halftone silhouette strip along the bottom; and one narrow cream caption footer. Overlap the layers aggressively while preserving a thin outer margin and clear face, prop, headline shape, and footer.

Give the hero and prop irregular pasted-sticker edges with a broad cream contour and thin dark or orange keyline. Use direct warm frontal flash, bright highlights, saturated mids, deep crisp shadows, and mild posterization. Keep depth flat and collage-like.

Use approximately 55 percent warm cream #F0DFC1, 30 percent burnt tangerine #E66D22, and 15 percent near-black #211B1A in the graphic system, with white knockout marks and only controlled saturated accents inside the photographic cutout. Add intentional coarse Ben-Day dots, photocopy grain, dry ink, mild edge wear, subtle screenprint misregistration, simplified technical diagrams, dotted fields, and clipped archival marks. Preserve crisp focal detail.

Render {MAIN_TEXT} exactly as supplied in extra-heavy condensed uppercase sans, tightly tracked and partly hidden behind the hero. Render {SECONDARY_TEXT} exactly as supplied only in a tiny upper-left kicker and italic footer. Use {ACCENT_SYMBOL} once as a sparse original emblem. Invent no other labels, numbers, logos, or copy. The black brush fragment and orange loop must be original abstract gestures and must not resemble a real signature.

For 4:5, stack the hero above the full-width base strip. For 5:4, widen the headline and diagram field, retain the hero near center-right, and extend the prop and loop laterally while keeping the same hierarchy. The result must feel celebratory, youthful, kinetic, handmade, and magazine-editorial. Match this visual system first, then make the new subject, action, prop, setting, text, and story unmistakably different.
